        "reproof": "Scope-ordering lane has a separately active actor-successor case; no mocked admission success."
      },
      {
        "id": "HS03-S2-WINDOW-ARCHIVE",
        "origin": "Design R-E/E4 requires range/digest and first/last capture clocks. actor_process1353 drops these; runtime_liveness395 emits the five old payload fields. Cold owners authenticate event bytes but never the referenced stdout bytes.",
        "whyPriorChecksMissed": "The selection assumed an existing general cold archive checker. Tests observed live transport integrity; the actual checker is private to no_output construction recovery. Neither validates the promised current window through cold acquisition.",
        "selectedRepair": "Carry the window offset/length/digest/first-last capture times and separate last qualifying activity from transport through actor and one declared event variant. Extract/reuse the existing range/digest computation and ordinary archive binding/path owner; do not duplicate a new parser/store/validator framework. Validate referenced window bytes once at the existing shared cold decode/adoption boundary for reopen, recover and direct cold reads, including applicable byte-array sibling. Pure fold and warm active selection do no archive reads.",
        "reproof": "Missing/changed/truncated referenced bytes refuse on actual cold owner paths; archive fsync-before-reference and failure/no-reference remain. Warm work counters do not gain checks."
      },
      {
        "id": "HS03-S2-PROFILE-COMPATIBILITY",
        "origin": "Contract table hashes include payload keys. S2 only recognizes L and latest3bcc; changing keys is not digest-neutral. Root imported actual immutable RC6 and frozen S2 builds: RC6 current5b35 differs already because D5 removes lifecycle copies and adds configuredIdentity.",
        "selectedRepair": "One existing profile owner selects the exact table and independent semantic capabilities. Preserve exact L fc3a, RC6 stamped5b35 (copied lifecycle/probes), S2 stamped3bcc (copy-free/probes), and prospective W (copy-free/window witness). No digest-not-latest => L shortcut, restamp, weakened checks or blanket archive obligation on old rows. New RC7 working stores use W. Preserve prior witnessed L transition identities; no P-to-W migration or native continuation on old P is selected in this bounded task.",
        "reproof": "Hard-pinned old contract digests and original per-chunk rows/event IDs/payloads survive cold reading and applicable fold/call projection. New W refs obey their new contract; undeclared/malformed profile/window combinations refuse."
      }
    ],
